      "side": 1,
      "message": "So it turns out that all of this logic (that was in ResourceProvider), is equivalent to what `SamplerDesc` is already doing to pack into its own internal `uint32_t fDesc` field.\n\nThis is a good opportunity to simplify this to something like:\n - expose a `uint32_t desc() const;` function in SamplerDesc to get at those bits so backends can store it in a resource key.\n - update `makeSamplerKey` to be virtual, with the default impl. basically like what\u0027s in `finishSamplerKey` except that the base info comes from the `SamplerDesc` directly.\n - remove `finishSamplerKey` so the key building happens in a single function call.\n \nThen vulkan and dawn backends that override `makeSamplerKey` can just store the desc bits + the ycbcr bits",
